\\sin \\theta.$", "This implies that $\\tan \\theta = 1.$", "This means that $\\theta$ must be an odd multiple of $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ in the given intervals.", "So, the only solutions are $\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}$ and $\\frac{7 \\pi}{4}.$", "# Answer\n\n\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}, \\frac{7 \\pi}{4}"], "pre_generated_answer": "\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}, \\frac{7 \\pi}{4}", "pre_generated_verifier_score": 0.0040077709615070865}, "label": {"steps": [{"completions": [{"text": "This problem involves logarithms, trigonometry, and inequalities.", "rating": 0, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "I need to recall the definition of logarithms, some basic properties of logarithms, and some trigonometric identities.", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "The definition of logarithms says that $\\log_b a = c$ if and only if $b^c = a.$", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "So, I can rewrite the given equation as $\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\sin 2 \\theta\\right)^{1/2} = \\sin \\theta.$", "rating": 1, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "This might make it easier to work with.", "rating": 0, "flagged": null}], "human_completion": null, "chosen_completion": 0}, {"completions": [{"text": "Now, I need to recall some basic properties of logarithms, such as the fact that $\\log_b a = c$ implies that $a$ and $b$ must have the same sign and $b \\neq 1.$", "rating": -1, "flagged": null}, {"text": "To simplify the left-hand side, I can use the property that $b^{1/2} = \\sqrt{b}$ for any positive $b.$", "rating": 0, "flagged": false}, {"text": "Now, I notice that the base of the logarithm is $\\frac{1}{2} \\sin 2 \\theta,$ which must be positive and not equal to 1 for the logarithm to be defined.", "rating": 1, "flagged": false}, {"text": "To simplify the le