quare is 36, and I need to find two other perfect squares that add up to 45. There are two ways to do this, and they are to use 25 and 20, or 9 and 36, but 20 is not a perfect square, so only the second way is valid.", "The next largest perfect square is 25, and I need to find two other perfect squares that add up to 56. There are two ways to do this, and they are to use 16 and 40, or 4 and 52, but neither 40 nor 52 are perfect squares, so neither way is valid.", "The next largest perfect square is 16, and I need to find two other perfect squares that add up to 65. There are two ways to do this, and they are to use 9 and 56, or 1 and 64, but 56 is not a perfect square, so only the second way is valid.", "The next largest perfect square is 9, and I need to find two other perfect squares that add up to 72. There are two ways to do this, and they are to use 4 and 68, or 1 and 71, but neither 68 nor 71 are perfect squares, so neither way is valid.", "The next largest perfect square is 4, and I need to find two other perfect squares that add up to 77. There are two ways to do this, and they are to use 1 and 76, or 0 and 77, but 76 is not a perfect square, and 0 is not a positive integer, so neither way is valid.", "The smallest perfect square is 1, and I need to find two other perfect squares that add up to 80. There are two ways to do this, and they are to use 1 and 79, or 0 and 80, but 79 is not a perfect square, and 0 is not a positive integer, so neither way is valid.", "Therefore, I have found only four valid ways to write 81 as the sum of three positive perfect squares, and they are: 49 + 16 + 16, 36 + 9 + 36, 16 + 1 + 64, and 4 + 4 + 73.", "# Answer\n\n4"], "pre_generated_answer": "4", "pre_generated_verifier_score": 0.007656099386789883}, "label": {"steps": [{"completions": [{"text": "To approach this problem, I need to think of all the possible positive perfect squares that are less than or equal to 81, since any larger perfect square would make the sum exceed 8